{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And you shall keep to do what is good</b>. Behold, He commands you that you shall keep to do what is good for you. \"A land flowing with milk and honey\" is joined to <b>to possess it</b> (Deuteronomy 6:1). And if it [the connection] is far-fetched, or perhaps the בֵּית [the letter bet] is elided, as in בֵּית ה' (II Kings 12:11) — this is the opinion of R. Abraham ibn Ezra (on Deuteronomy 6:3). And if so, the verse would further be missing from <b>and you multiply greatly</b> the word \"in it\" or \"on its account.\" But there is no need for this, for <b>so that your days may be long</b> continues from here, and its meaning is <b>so that it may be good for you</b>. Or the word <b>אֲשֶׁר</b> itself functions in this way, as in וַיָּסֶר מִגְּבִירָה אֲשֶׁר עָשְׂתָה מִפֶּלֶץ (I Kings 15:13) — on account of what she did; and similarly בַּאֲשֶׁר אַתְּ אִשְׁתּוֹ (Genesis 39:9) — on account of your being his wife; and likewise the verse אֲשֶׁר אָנֹכִי מְצַוְּךָ הַיּוֹם אֲשֶׁר יִיטַב לְךָ וגו' וּלְמַעַן תַּאֲרִיךְ יָמִים עַל הָאֲדָמָה (Deuteronomy 4:40). And the delimitation of the verse is: \"And you shall hear, O Israel, and you shall keep to do, so that it may be good for you, and so that you may multiply greatly, as YHWH, the Elohim of your fathers, spoke to give you a land flowing with milk and honey, etc.\" — meaning, so that it may be good for you when He gives you a good and spacious land, as He says below (Deuteronomy 6:18), לְמַעַן אֲשֶׁר יִיטַב לָךְ וּבָאתָ וְיָרַשְׁתָּ אֶת הָאָרֶץ. And similar to it: וַיִּתֶּן לוֹ בַּיִת וָלֶחֶם אָמַר לוֹ (I Kings 11:18)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The Hebrew word מִפֶּלֶץ in the I Kings 15:13 citation appears as מִפְלֶצֶת in many editions of the Ramban and in the biblical text; the reading here follows the Hebrew as given in the source. Ramban's citation of I Kings 15:13 is paraphrastic rather than verbatim."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:46:13.331544350Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}